text: |-
  Sam Parker
  @BasedSamParker
  BREAKING: UVU has denied our GRAMA request for the camera footage
  from behind Charlie's tent. This is the camera that captured the actions
  & reactions of Mikey McCoy, Blake Neff, Terryl Farnsworth and others
  after Charlie was shot & they fled the scene. UVU says to reveal this
  footage would jeopardize public safety and endanger enforcement
  proceedings, investigations & someone's right to a fair trial. I wonder,
  how would revealing this footage endanger anyone's safety or a fair trial
  for Tyler Robinson?
  eras located at or near ine pedestrian runner
  under Campus Drive (connecting off-campus
  housing areas such as The Green on Campus
  Drive to central campus facilities) on
  September 10, 2025, from 12:00 PM MDT to
  6:00 PM MDT. This includes footage from
  entry/exit points of the tunnel, adjacent path-
  ways, and any overlapping campus security
  cameras that may capture activity in this
  Records created or maintained for civil, crimi-
  nal, or administrative enforcement purposes
  where their release could reasonably be ex-
  pected to interfere with enforcement pro-
  ceedings or investigations or deprive a per-
  son of a right to a fair trial.
  3. Utah Code Ann. § 63G-2-106: Records of se-
  curity measures (security plans and
  procedures).
  Camelot Jack
  Commentary account
  Replying to @CamelotJack1963
  Request denied
  Appeal will be filed
  @CamelotJack1963 • 2h
  "All surveillance video footage (including raw,
  unedited files in their highest available reso-
  lution) captured by any and all security cam-
  eras located at or near the Pedestrian Tunnel
  under Campus Drive (connecting off-campus
  housing areas such as The Green on Campus
  Drive to central campus facilities) on
  September 10, 2025, from 12:00 PM MDT to
  6:00 PM MDT. This includes footage from
  entry/exit points of the tunnel, adjacent path-
  ways, and any overlapping campus security
  cameras that may capture activity in this
  area.
  Any associated metadata, timestamps, or logs
  related to the above footage, including cam-
  era activation records, motion detection
  alerts, or export histories for the specified
  1. Utah Code Ann. § 63G-2 305(12): Disclosure
  would jeopardize the security of public prop-
  erty, buildings, or systems.
  2. Utah Code Ann. § 63G-2-305(10)(a)-(c):
  Records created or maintained for civil, crimi-
  nal, or administrative enforcement purposes
  where their release could reasonably be ex-
  pected to interfere with enforcement pro-
  ceedings or investigations or deprive a per-
  son of a right to a fair trial.
  3. Utah Code Ann. § 63G-2-106: Records of se-
  curity measures (security plans and
  procedures).
  You have the right to appeal this determina-
  tion to the Chief Administrative Officer of
  Utah Valley University. A written appeal must
  be filed within 30 davs after the date of this
